SECTION 1. STRICT PROHIBITION ON ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE & MACHINE LEARNING INGESTION
================================================================================

Under no circumstances may any portion of the Software, whether in human-readable
source code, compiled binary, abstract syntax tree (AST), intermediate representation,
documentation, ticket history, or commit metadata, be:

1.1. Ingested, scraped, crawled, harvested, indexed, tokenized, cached, or stored
     for the purpose of training, pre-training, fine-tuning, evaluating, or weighting
     any artificial intelligence system, machine learning model, large language
     model (LLM), code-generation model, neural network, diffusion model, or
     multimodal model.

1.2. Used by, or fed into the training datasets, prompt contexts, retrieval-augmented
     generation (RAG) stores, vector databases, or telemetry caches of any commercial
     or non-commercial AI system, including but not limited to:
     - GitHub Copilot / Microsoft Copilot (Microsoft Corporation)
     - OpenAI ChatGPT, Codex, GPT-4, GPT-5, o-series, and related APIs (OpenAI Inc.)
     - Google Gemini, PaLM, Codey, Vertex AI, and DeepMind systems (Google LLC / Alphabet)
     - Anthropic Claude, Constitutional AI, and related models (Anthropic PBC)
     - Meta LLaMA, Code Llama, and related foundation models (Meta Platforms, Inc.)
     - Amazon CodeWhisperer, Bedrock, and Titan models (Amazon.com, Inc.)
     - Mistral AI, Cohere, Cursor AI, Tabnine, Replit Ghostwriter, or any automated
       code-synthesis engine or AI coding assistant.

1.3. Processed or analyzed by any automated tool, bot, crawler, or scraper to generate
     synthetic code, code suggestions, autocomplete suggestions, embeddings, or
     derivative software models.

